Version 4
SHEET 1 880 680
WIRE 0 64 -32 64
WIRE 192 64 64 64
WIRE 0 80 -32 80
WIRE 144 80 64 80
WIRE 0 96 -32 96
WIRE 96 96 64 96
WIRE 144 96 144 80
WIRE 192 96 192 64
WIRE -32 128 -32 112
FLAG -32 128 0
FLAG 96 160 0
FLAG 144 160 0
FLAG 192 160 0
SYMBOL v_3phase -64 64 R0
WINDOW 3 -54 55 Left 0
SYMATTR Value U1Nenn=400k FREQU=50 Texp=0m TD=0 dphi=0
SYMATTR InstName U1
SYMBOL impedance 32 64 R0
SYMATTR InstName U2
SYMBOL cap 80 96 R0
WINDOW 3 -16 77 Left 2
SYMATTR Value {290nF*length}
SYMATTR InstName C1
SYMBOL cap 128 96 R0
WINDOW 3 -11 47 Left 2
SYMATTR Value {290nF*length}
SYMATTR InstName C2
SYMBOL cap 176 96 R0
WINDOW 3 -13 75 Left 2
SYMATTR Value {290nF*length}
SYMATTR InstName C3
TEXT -80 8 Left 2 !.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}\n.options vntol=1m abstol=1m reltol=0.001
TEXT -80 32 Left 2 !.tran 0 1 0 0.01m
TEXT -16 48 Left 2 !.param rn=0.4 ln={4/314.159} length=2
TEXT 80 192 Left 2 ;HINT: Energy is always ALT/(ALT Gr)+Click before CTRL+Click\n ( NOTE: ALT+click on german keyboard layout often crash LTspice\nPlease use ALT Gr + Click for german keyboards )\nE1(phase1)=C*U*U = 30933.3 (can also be integrated with V(N002)*I(C3) from 990ms to 995ms=Halvewave of the power)\nE2 (phase2+3)=2*C*(U/2)*(U/2)=15466.7\nE=E1+E2=46400J=46.4kJ (Energy stored in the line capacitances of the 2km cable)\nCTRL+Click on trace expression in waveformviewer\n -> (only small amount of energy saved\n    in line capacitances in contrast to the high energy in the incuctive shorted case)
TEXT -80 144 Left 2 ;Also look at \ncapacitive_energy.wxmx
TEXT 8 120 Left 0 ;Capacity of a 400kV line with 1200mm2 square area \nand a lenghts of 2km \nInductance is neglected
TEXT -80 168 Left 1 ;Note:\nIn line capacitances\nand in cbatt and in lbatt models or transformers\nonly small amounts of energy are stored\nbut in short circuit case a high amount\nof energy is stored in the inductivities\nSee same example in this directory
TEXT 232 152 Left 2 ;oil_u400_o1200mm2 2km length
TEXT 280 160 Left 2 ;see also Youtube example MyFirstExample.asc
LINE Normal 224 176 272 160 2
